      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T23:39:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`enableSwbCodec` calls `mNativeInterface.enableSwb`, then calls `enableSwbNative`, then calls `sBluetoothHfpInterface-\u003eEnableSwb`, then calls `enable_aptx_swb_codec`, which is a function to read init flag and whether that devices supports LC3\n```\nbt_status_t enable_aptx_swb_codec(bool enable, RawAddress* bd_addr) {\n  if (bluetooth::common::init_flags::aptx_voice_is_enabled() \u0026\u0026\n      (get_lc3_swb_codec_status(bd_addr) \u003d\u003d false)) {\n    LOG_INFO(\"%d\", enable);\n    aptx_swb_codec_status \u003d enable;\n    return BT_STATUS_SUCCESS;\n  }\n  return BT_STATUS_FAIL;\n}\n```\nthis might be better to not handled in Java layer, instead, to use or not to use aptx would be better to handle on native layer during feature exchange.\nFor the dependency on network info, please see [comment#309](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/2678015/16/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/telephony/BluetoothCall.java#309)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1199,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1199,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "0315ebeeb2aa0d3dfc71dc443f989940fb689fe9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
